Vacuum unlinks the source without syncing the directory after the rename:
a power cut can keep the unlink and lose the rename, and the next open
deletes the compacted copy as staging. Reverts #200's vacuum site (#199).
Guarded-by: "directory sync: a failed sync in vacuum keeps the source"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/db_vacuum.cpp b/bytecaskdb/db_vacuum.cpp
index 056e1d5..53f3625 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/db_vacuum.cpp
+++ b/bytecaskdb/db_vacuum.cpp
@@ -323,7 +323,7 @@ auto DB::vacuum_compact_file(std::uint32_t file_id, std::uint64_t retain_after)
   // The source is unlinked once this commits. Were that unlink durable and
   // the rename not, the next open would find only .data.tmp, delete it as
   // staging, and lose every live entry the source held.
-  sync_directory(dir_, "io_dir_sync_vacuum");
+  (void)dir_;
 #ifdef BYTECASK_TESTING
   // *Orphaned .data files* in docs/correctness_validation.md: the rename
   // completed and the commit did not. The compacted file is on disk under its
